<title>JAPAN: Okinawa Sekiyu to shut topper March 10 - April 17.</title>
<headline>Okinawa Sekiyu to shut topper March 10 - April 17.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Okinawa Sekiyu Seisei Co Ltd said on Tuesday it plans to close its 110,000 barrel-per-day crude distillation unit on Japan's southernmost major island of Okinawa on March 10 for routine maintenance checks.</p>
<p>The topper will resume operations on April 18.</p>
<p>Okinawa Sekiyu is wholly owned by major refiner Idemitsu Kosan Co Ltd.</p>
</text>
